   datasets, benchmark collections, or synthetic data
   derived from covered materials.

c. Populate a shared or commercial retrieval system,
   vector database, knowledge service, or AI content
   library.

d. Provide covered materials as persistent knowledge
   for a chatbot, assistant, agent, or automated
   educational service.

e. Generate substitutes for the repository's lessons,
   exercises, books, diagrams, or other publications
   for redistribution or commercial use.

f. Upload covered materials to a third-party AI service,
   including through prompts, attachments, retrieval
   connectors, or automated ingestion.

The personal study permission permits private analysis
using a locally operated model only when:

i. The materials remain private and are not transmitted
   to a third-party service.

ii. The activity does not train or improve a model.

iii. Resulting outputs containing or adapting covered
     materials remain private.

iv. All other conditions of this license are followed.

These restrictions apply only to covered materials.
